## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: bạn xử lý ghi dữ liệu khi ngoại tuyến như thế nào.**

> *"Reads offline are the easy half — you persist the cache and serve stale data with a timestamp so the user knows what they're looking at.*
> *Writes are the interesting part. I queue mutations instead of failing them, and replay them when the connection comes back. Two details make that actually work.*
> *First, the queue has to survive the app being closed. Functions can't be serialised to disk, only keys, so each mutation needs a key registered with a default handler — otherwise the queue looks fine until the user force-quits, and then their pending changes are silently gone.*
> *Second, retries need to be idempotent. If a write reaches the server but the response is lost on the way back, the client thinks it failed and sends it again — and now you've got a duplicate. I generate the ID on the client and use an upsert, so replaying the same operation any number of times produces one row.*
> *For conflicts I went with last-write-wins, because it's a single-user app and the only conflict is the same person on two devices. I wrote that decision down with the reasoning. If it were shared or financial data I'd want server-wins or an explicit merge instead."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `replay` (v) | phát lại, gửi lại | *Replay them when the connection comes back.* |
| `survive` (v) | sống sót qua | *The queue has to survive a force-quit.* |
| `silently` (adv) | âm thầm, không báo | *Their changes are silently gone.* |
| `idempotent` (adj) | lặp lại vẫn cùng kết quả | *Retries need to be idempotent.* |
| `duplicate` (n) | bản trùng | *Now you've got a duplicate.* |

